PART 11 – SECURITY, PRIVACY AND CLINICAL SAFEGUARDS

This application handles sensitive patient, employee and financial information.

Implement:

- Role-based access control.
- Server-side authorization.
- Secure cookies.
- Password hashing.
- Rate limiting.
- CSRF protection appropriate to cookie authentication.
- Input validation.
- Output escaping.
- SQL parameterization.
- Secure file access.
- Upload MIME and size validation.
- Session expiration.
- Audit logging.
- Consent records.
- Sensitive record access history.
- Account deactivation.
- Password reset.
- Backup and restore procedures.
- Error handling without exposing secrets.

Clinical safeguards:

- Never invent patient diagnoses.
- Never invent laboratory results.
- Never generate prescriptions automatically without authorized clinician action.
- Do not expose unreleased reports.
- Do not allow unauthorized edits to finalized clinical records.
- Preserve historical records.
- Record who created, modified and reviewed clinical information.

Financial safeguards:

- Never store raw card data.
- Record transaction references.
- Audit financial changes.
- Prevent duplicate payment records.
- Keep clinical and financial permissions separate.

Compliance must be assessed against applicable local laws and hospital policies before production deployment. Do not claim HIPAA, DPDP or other compliance certification merely because security features exist.

